(614,"城郭・歴史","Castle · History"),
(615,"1702年に築かれた、島内で最も保存状態のよい城郭。","Built in 1702, the best-preserved castle on the island."),
(616,"光瀨城は1702年、白令海戦争の終結後に大祁宣武皇帝の命で築かれました。戦後の秩序再建の象徴であり、海峡航路を治める拠点でもありました。三百年以上を経た今も、幾重にも重なる天守、曲輪と石垣、白壁と灰色の瓦の回廊の大半が当時のまま残り、島内で最も保存状態のよい城郭です。","Hikarise Castle was built in 1702 by order of Emperor Xuanwu of Daqi after the Bering Sea War, as a symbol of postwar order and a stronghold controlling the strait routes. After more than three centuries, its tiers of keeps, baileys and stone walls, and its white-walled, gray-tiled corridors remain largely as they were—the best-preserved castle on the island."),
(617,"高みから眺めると、白壁と黒い木格子、灰色の瓦が松林と庭園のあいだに幾重にも広がります。晴れた日には天守の金の鯱が空の下で輝き、霧の朝は雲海に浮かぶようです。船井大島駅から堀沿いに城門へ向かう道は、写真に最適な場所ばかりです。","From the heights, white walls, black wooden lattices and gray tiles spread in layers between pine groves and gardens. On clear days the golden shachi on the keep gleams under the sky; on misty mornings the castle seems to float on a sea of clouds. The walk along the moat from Funai-Oshima station to the gate offers great photo angles all the way."),
(618,"1702年築、大祁宣武皇帝が白令海戦争後に建立","Built in 1702 by Emperor Xuanwu of Daqi after the Bering Sea War"),
(619,"島内で最も保存状態のよい城郭","The best-preserved castle on the island"),
(620,"天守・石垣・白壁と瓦葺の回廊","Keep, stone walls, white walls and tiled corridors"),
(621,"霧の朝も晴れた日の天守も、それぞれの趣","Misty mornings and sunny-day keeps each have their charm"),
(622,"朝霧の中の光瀨城天守と城郭","The keep and castle of Hikarise in morning mist"),
(623,"朝霧の中の天守と城郭","The keep and castle in morning mist"),
(624,"光瀨城の瓦屋根と回廊を見下ろす","Looking down on Hikarise Castle’s tiled roofs and corridors"),
(625,"幾重にも重なる瓦屋根と回廊","Layered tiled roofs and corridors"),
(626,"かつもりぎょこう","Katsumori-gyoko"),
(627,"港・グルメ","Port · Food"),
(628,"日の出と朝市、獲れたての海の幸の港町。","A port town of sunrises, morning markets and fresh-caught seafood."),
(629,"勝守漁港は光瀨都市圏で最も海に近い駅です。夜が明けると漁船が次々と着岸し、港は朝日に金色に染まります。日の出を眺めるのにぴったりで、岸辺の朝市もにぎわい、獲れたての魚が箱ごと店先に並びます。","Katsumori Fishing Port is the closest station to the sea in the Hikarise area. As day breaks, fishing boats come in one after another and the harbor turns gold in the morning light—a fine spot for sunrise. The morning market on the quay comes alive, with boxes of fresh fish carried to the stalls."),
(630,"市場周辺の食堂や小さな店では、その日に獲れた海の幸が味わえます。刺身、海鮮丼、焼き魚、温かい汁物。早い電車で来て、朝食をとってから港をのんびり歩くのがおすすめです。高架線路は港の後ろにあり、待ち時間に港の向こうを走る列車も眺められます。","Diners and small shops around the market serve the day’s catch: sashimi, seafood bowls, grilled fish and hot soup. Take an early train, have breakfast, then stroll the harbor. The elevated tracks run behind the port, so you can watch trains pass while you wait."),
(631,"日の出と朝市","Sunrise and morning market"),
(632,"獲れたての海の幸、海鮮丼","Fresh seafood and seafood bowls"),
(633,"漁船と港の景色","Fishing boats and harbor views"),
(634,"早い電車での訪問がおすすめ","An early train is recommended"),
(635,"勝守漁港の漁船と、奥の高架駅","Fishing boats at Katsumori Fishing Port with the elevated station beyond"),
(636,"港の漁船、その奥に高架線路と駅","Boats in the harbor, with elevated tracks and a station beyond"),
(637,"あまとりざきじんじゃ","Amatorizaki-jinja"),
(638,"神社・海岸","Shrine · Coast"),
(639,"海に面した神社。夕暮れの夕日と参道が一番の見どころ。","A shrine facing the sea. Sunset and the approach road are the highlights."),
(640,"天鳥崎神社は海岸沿いにあり、参拝者は参道を歩いて鳥居と社殿へ向かいます。潮風が道のりのあいだずっと寄り添います。","Amatorizaki Shrine stands on the coast; worshippers walk the approach road to the torii and shrine buildings, accompanied by salty sea breezes all the way."),
(641,"夕方は最も魅力的な時間帯です。夕日が海面と屋根瓦を橙赤色に染め、社殿のシルエットが空に浮かびます。参拝のあとは参道に戻って、沿道の小さな店をのぞき、電車で帰るのもよいでしょう。天鳥崎中央駅から歩いて行けます。","Evening is the most enchanting time: the setting sun paints the sea and roof tiles orange-red and the shrine’s silhouette stands against the sky. After worship, return along the approach road, browse the small shops, then take the train home. It is a walk from Tentori-Chuo station."),
(642,"海岸と夕日","Coast and sunset"),
(643,"神社と参道","Shrine and approach road"),
(644,"夕方の訪問がおすすめ","Best visited toward evening"),
(645,"天鳥崎中央駅から徒歩で行けます","Walkable from Tentori-Chuo station"),
(646,"夕日に橙赤色に染まる駅舎と電車","Station building and train glowing orange-red in the sunset"),
(647,"夕日の天鳥崎周辺","Amatorizaki area at sunset"),
(648,"ひかりせしりつはくぶつかん","Hikarise-shiritsu-hakubutsukan"),
(649,"博物館・文化","Museum · Culture"),
(650,"歴史、鉄道、都市の発展史、港町の文物をまとめて見られます。","See history, railways, urban development and port-town artifacts all at once."),
(651,"光瀨市立博物館はガラスのカーテンウォールの建物と球形の展示ホールが特徴で、光瀨の歴史、鉄道の発展、都市が成長してきた軌跡、港町に長年蓄積された文物を展示しています。","Hikarise City Museum is known for its glass curtain-wall building and spherical exhibition hall, displaying Hikarise’s history, the development of its railways, the city’s growth, and artifacts accumulated over the years in the port town."),
(652,"この街が城下町と港からどのように今日の鉄道都市へ発展したのかを知るなら、ここから始めるのが一番分かりやすいでしょう。雨の日や、ゆっくり過ごしたい午後の予定にも向いています。ひがしいち駅から歩いて行けます。","To learn how this city grew from a castle town and port into today’s railway metropolis, this is the clearest place to start. It also suits rainy days or a relaxed afternoon. A walk from Higashi-ichi station."),
(653,"歴史・鉄道・都市の発展史","History, railways and urban development"),
(654,"港町の文物","Port-town artifacts"),
